   {
    "name": "show_image",
    "description": "Shows an image file to the user, inline in their terminal. Accepts PNG, JPEG, WebP, GIF and TIFF.\n\nUse it without being asked whenever you have made or changed something visual, before you say the work is done: screenshot a page or component with headless Playwright, or show a design concept, chart, slide or generated image. Do this instead of asking the user to open a file or a localhost URL. Don't use it when nothing visual changed.\n\nWhen the image shows work you changed, also pass `changes` (what you changed, a few words each) and `compare` (an image of the same view from before the change), so the user can switch between Original, Updated and Compare. Pass `summary` only for checks you actually ran. When you show a new version of something you showed earlier, pass `previous` with its #id so both stay in the same history.\n\nThe image goes to the user's screen, not to you. Read the file yourself only if you need to check it.\n\nSave screenshots and recordings you make to show here in a temporary folder, such as $TMPDIR or /tmp, not in the project. Save them in the project only when the user asks to keep them, or when the project already has a folder for them, such as one for test screenshots."
   },
   {
    "name": "show_video",
    "description": "Plays a video file to the user, inline in their terminal, in a player that starts on its own. Accepts MP4, MOV, WebM and GIF.\n\nUse it without being asked to show recordings: after building or fixing an interactive feature, record a headless Playwright run that clicks through it and play that, rather than asking the user to try it themselves. Also use it for animations and for ad or film cuts you have made.\n\nWhen the video shows work you changed, pass `changes`, each with `at` (the second it appears), and `checks` for what you tested, also with `at`. For a fix, record the same steps on the old version and pass that file as `compare` with its own `compare_checks`; the two play side by side, in sync. Pass `summary` only for checks you actually ran, and `previous` with an earlier #id when this is a new version of something you showed.\n\nKeep clips short: they are played as frames, at most 900 at up to 12 per second. You do not see the video.\n\nSave screenshots and recordings you make to show here in a temporary folder, such as $TMPDIR or /tmp, not in the project. Save them in the project only when the user asks to keep them, or when the project already has a folder for them, such as one for test screenshots."
   }
